# Editing the Cross-Platform Headers

When editing **Shared/NtlSharedCommon.h** or **Shared/Util/NtlPortable.h**:

- **Structure**: Keep `#ifdef _WIN32` / `#else` in NtlSharedCommon.h; keep `#if !defined(_WIN32)` / `#else` in NtlPortable.h. Do not invert or mix platform branches.
- **New APIs**: Prefer macros for new compatibility so one definition covers all call sites. Use the same macro/API name on both platforms.
- **Parity**: When adding something for Linux, ensure the Windows side has the same symbol (or already provides it). When adding for Windows, add the Linux equivalent in the `#else` block.
